WEBVTT

00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:04.309
Import and Migration gives administrators a place to review external data

00:00:04.349 --> 00:00:05.949
before saving it into Resgrid.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.180
The existing Academy CSV Practice workspace is Reviewing, with Add

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.029
to a live department as its mode.

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:17.090
The separate Start an import form explains the choice between a new

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.030
department and one already working.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:24.149
Use Resume for an existing workspace so its files and decisions stay together.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:27.059
Overview separates preparation from results.

00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:32.510
This fictional workspace has two Rows checked, two Ready to import, zero

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.010
Imported and zero People to invite.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.109
Its progress list still has later work to do.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.770
Use these counts to understand what has happened before deciding the next step.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:47.350
A ready data set has passed its current checks; those rows have not

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.830
yet been added to the department.

00:00:49.069 --> 00:00:50.880
Open Files and data sets.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:55.739
Upload a file accepts formats such as CSV, Excel and JSON.

00:00:56.159 --> 00:01:01.260
The existing training CSV is listed as Stations and groups with two ready rows.

00:01:01.689 --> 00:01:05.849
On the right, D4H Team Manager supplies terminology context.

00:01:06.189 --> 00:01:10.580
Selecting a source product helps explain names; Resgrid still reads

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.259
and matches the uploaded file.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:17.249
Expand Glossary to compare In D4H Team Manager with In Resgrid.

00:01:17.699 --> 00:01:22.249
Members correspond to People, and Groups correspond to Stations and groups.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.429
Equipment is marked Inventory, not imported.

00:01:25.839 --> 00:01:28.549
Incidents is marked Calls, not imported.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.100
Read those limits when planning a migration.

00:01:31.459 --> 00:01:35.569
A familiar product name or suggested label does not mean every kind of

00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:37.370
historical data will be transferred.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:42.039
The Resgrid starter workbook offers a sheet for each kind of data, with example

00:01:42.039 --> 00:01:44.270
rows and choices based on the department.

00:01:44.699 --> 00:01:48.320
Visible options include Statuses, Certification types,

00:01:48.559 --> 00:01:50.639
Stations and groups, and Roles.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.659
Choose a scope that matches the data being prepared.

00:01:54.249 --> 00:01:57.919
Farther down, Download workbook provides the selected layout.

00:01:58.419 --> 00:02:03.509
Individual CSV templates are available for Stations and groups, People and Units.

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:07.270
Download current data provides existing department data in the

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.380
same layout for review and editing.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:14.290
These are the actual download controls; this lesson reviews them without claiming

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.540
a new downloaded or reimported file.

00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:19.699
Open the training data set and review Match columns.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.690
Its destination is Stations and groups.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:26.929
TeamName maps to Name, and TeamCategory maps to Type.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.869
Check the sample values and ask whether they mean the

00:02:29.869 --> 00:02:31.549
same thing in the destination.

00:02:31.999 --> 00:02:35.459
Keep the columns the department needs, rather than treating a confident

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:37.359
suggestion as the final decision.

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:41.849
StationLatitude and StationLongitude show paired numeric samples

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:43.070
for the training location.

00:02:43.449 --> 00:02:44.469
Review them together.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.720
Same value for every row is a separate option for a shared value

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.750
when the file has no suitable column.

00:02:51.119 --> 00:02:53.349
Its visible address fields remain blank.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:57.509
A shared default should describe the whole data set, rather than assigning

00:02:57.509 --> 00:02:59.919
one site's details to unrelated teams.

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:05.199
Match values, Belongs to, makes the proposed hierarchy easier to inspect.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.420
Firehouse 51 is selected for one value.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:13.119
The in-file Academy Ops reference remains Not decided on this page.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.629
Check each relationship against the intended organization

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.579
before using Save choices.

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:22.819
This recording reviews the current choices; it does not resolve or

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:24.670
save the undecided reference.

00:03:25.039 --> 00:03:27.950
Both the names and the resulting hierarchy matter.

00:03:28.119 --> 00:03:30.859
Open Issues and confirm the selected scope.

00:03:31.339 --> 00:03:35.690
All data sets is selected, and the page currently reports No issues.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.550
Show resolved issues is available for earlier corrections.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:42.479
This is the status of the checks for this workspace.

00:03:42.899 --> 00:03:47.090
The destination, relationship and change-preview reviews still matter.

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:51.069
Here no issue is corrected and no import is committed.

00:03:51.339 --> 00:03:55.589
Configure shows proposed department settings alongside the imported data.

00:03:56.089 --> 00:04:00.160
Will be changed is zero, and Waiting for your decision is two.

00:04:00.719 --> 00:04:03.460
Names contains the suggestions in this example.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.980
Review them before using Accept all suggestions, because configuration

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.720
can affect the words members see across the department.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.550
The proposals rename Calls to Incidents and Personnel to Members.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:19.140
Accept and Decline let an administrator decide each one.

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:21.730
Both still have Suggested status.

00:04:22.189 --> 00:04:26.059
These terminology changes do not import incident history, create

00:04:26.059 --> 00:04:28.349
people, or establish who has joined.

00:04:28.829 --> 00:04:31.899
Useful names should reflect how a community response team,

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:36.199
search-and-rescue organization or security company actually works.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.379
Review and import summarizes the proposed write.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:40.780
Add is two.

00:04:41.209 --> 00:04:45.939
Update or link, Unchanged, Invite to join and Blocked are zero.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:50.109
The data-set row identifies Stations and groups and the training file,

00:04:50.349 --> 00:04:52.210
connecting the totals to their source.

00:04:52.549 --> 00:04:56.289
The large What will happen area is blank in this layout; use

00:04:56.289 --> 00:04:57.809
the visible counts and table.

00:04:58.219 --> 00:05:00.010
These remain proposed changes.

00:05:00.159 --> 00:05:03.890
How to treat records that already exist is set to Add only.

00:05:04.259 --> 00:05:08.909
The explanation says this mode never changes existing Resgrid records.

00:05:09.279 --> 00:05:13.609
It also explains that reviewed updates change approved fields and skip

00:05:13.609 --> 00:05:15.399
records edited since the preview.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.869
Recalculate the preview is available after a change.

00:05:19.219 --> 00:05:22.670
Check Data sets in this import so the mode and included files

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.250
agree with the intended work.

00:05:24.649 --> 00:05:27.289
This example leaves Add only unchanged.

00:05:27.469 --> 00:05:31.400
Please confirm states that zero people will be added, and imported

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:35.159
people cannot sign in or receive notifications until invited.

00:05:35.549 --> 00:05:37.309
The checkbox remains unchecked.

00:05:37.729 --> 00:05:42.250
The page also says approval requires confirmation with your second factor.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:46.499
Approve and import crosses from review into applying changes.

00:05:46.939 --> 00:05:49.460
This lesson stops its approval demonstration at

00:05:49.489 --> 00:05:51.019
those visible requirements.

00:05:51.319 --> 00:05:54.399
It does not approve this workspace or enroll a factor.

00:05:54.639 --> 00:05:57.730
Open History and read Run and Status together.

00:05:58.139 --> 00:06:01.599
The three retained runs are File check, each marked Done.

00:06:02.079 --> 00:06:05.839
They establish completed file checks, not a completed import.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:10.049
The generic background-work message below the table does not identify

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.740
another successful operation.

00:06:12.269 --> 00:06:16.949
Verify and activate separates People imported, Invited and Signed in.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:21.330
All are zero, and Invitations says No invitations yet.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:25.799
The Activation checklist still requires reviewing results and signing off.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.390
Sign off and go live is disabled.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:32.539
Done beside an empty invitation step does not show that anybody

00:06:32.539 --> 00:06:34.659
received an invitation or signed in.

00:06:35.089 --> 00:06:38.530
Plan result verification and member activation as distinct

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.909
work after the import.

00:06:40.109 --> 00:06:45.540
Return to Overview: two rows ready, zero imported and zero people to invite.

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:48.989
This is a review of an existing preparation workspace,

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:50.899
not a completed migration.

00:06:51.559 --> 00:06:53.840
Fire departments can start with station data.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:57.530
Community care and mental-health teams can review operational

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.469
groups without clinical histories.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.709
Search-and-rescue groups can check volunteer organization; security

00:07:03.709 --> 00:07:07.649
companies can review site groups; wildland contractors can plan

00:07:07.649 --> 00:07:11.819
seasonal teams; industrial responders can review facility groups.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.199
Begin with a small understood file, verify its meaning, and use the proposed

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:19.469
counts to guide the next authorized step.

